<% unless local_assigns[:hide_heading] %><h1>Cookies Policy</h1><% end %>
<p class="legal-subtitle">This policy explains how RxTerminal uses cookies when you access this portal.</p>

<section>
  <h2>1. What Are Cookies</h2>
  <p>Cookies are small text files placed on your device when you visit a website. They allow the site to recognise your device and remember certain preferences or session state. We use session cookies (which expire when you close your browser) and persistent cookies (which remain for a set period).</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>2. Cookies We Use</h2>

  <h3>2.1 Strictly Necessary Cookies</h3>
  <p>These cookies are essential for the application to function and cannot be disabled. They do not store any personally identifiable information.</p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Cookie</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Expires</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>_rxterminal_session</code></td><td>Maintains your authenticated session as a staff or manager user</td><td>Session</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>device_credentials</code></td><td>Stores encrypted kiosk device credentials for auto-login</td><td>1 year</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>device_token</code></td><td>Short-lived JWT token for kiosk device authentication</td><td>24 hours</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>privacy_accepted</code></td><td>Records whether a customer has accepted the privacy notice</td><td>Session</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>waiting_display_token</code></td><td>Keeps the waiting area display screen authenticated after staff log out, so the screen stays live without requiring a persistent login</td><td>30 days</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3>2.2 Functional Cookies</h3>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Cookie</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Expires</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>locale</code></td><td>Remembers your preferred language setting</td><td>1 year</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3>2.3 Analytics Cookies</h3>
  <p>RxTerminal does not currently use third-party analytics services within the application.</p>

  <h3>2.4 Marketing / Advertising Cookies</h3>
  <p>We do not use marketing or advertising cookies.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>3. Third-Party Cookies</h2>
  <p>RxTerminal does not embed third-party content such as social media widgets or video players that would set cookies from external domains on your device.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>4. How To Manage Cookies</h2>
  <p>You can control and delete cookies through your browser settings:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Google Chrome: <code>chrome://settings/cookies</code></li>
    <li>Mozilla Firefox: <code>about:preferences#privacy</code></li>
    <li>Microsoft Edge: <code>edge://settings/privacy</code></li>
    <li>Safari: Preferences &gt; Privacy</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Disabling strictly necessary cookies will prevent you from using core features of the application.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>5. Changes To This Policy</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy from time to time. Any changes will be posted at this location with an updated version date.</p>
</section>

